<%#
  The cart (CartController), in the site's frame (CartHelper draws it): a
  band of deep water with the title and how many items the cart holds;
  then, on the page's band, what the last change said, and the lines, each
  with its product's picture, its title (the link to its page), its price
  for one as the product publishes it now and what the line costs, a form
  for its quantity and one that takes it out; beside them, the total of
  the lines for sale and the checkout's button, or why there is none. A
  line whose product is out of stock, has no price or is gone says why and
  can only be taken out; the checkout leaves it out. An empty cart says so
  and leads to the shop. Every form posts to the cart's own addresses,
  with no token and no script: the Origin a browser sends is what lets it
  through.
  said: what the last change said, above the cart; priced: the cart priced
  (ShopRules.price_cart), nil for a request refused before the cart was
  read; shown: each line's page and picture (CartPage.shown); media: the
  library's items for those pictures; closed: why there is no checkout's
  button, or nil.
-%>
<%= cart_head("Your cart", priced && (priced.lines.empty? ? CartHelper::EMPTY : cart_count_words(priced.lines))) %><%= cart_body(priced, shown, media, currency, said: said, closed: closed, shop_path: shop_path) -%>
